@startuml

skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10
skinparam BoxPadding 10

title Loyalty Service - SAGA Pattern for Basket Pricing with Points Redemption

actor "Customer" as customer
participant "Shopping System\n(POS)" as pos
participant "API Gateway" as apiGw
box "Loyalty Service" #LightBlue
    participant "Basket Controller" as controller
    participant "Redemption Service\n(SAGA Orchestrator)" as saga
    participant "Balance Repository" as balanceRepo
    participant "Offer Repository" as offerRepo
    participant "Usage Repository" as usageRepo
    participant "Transaction Repository" as txRepo
end box
database "Loyalty DB\n(PostgreSQL)" as loyaltyDB

== SAGA Happy Path: Successful Redemption ==

customer -> pos: 1. Checkout with basket\nSelect redemption offers
pos -> apiGw: 2. POST /api/loyalty/basket/price\n{\n  customerId: {id},\n  basketReference: "{ref}",\n  selectedOfferIds: [{id1}, {id2}],\n  items: [...]\n}
apiGw -> controller: 3. Forward request (HTTP:8085)
controller -> saga: 4. priceBasketWithRedemption(request)
activate saga

note right of saga
  **SAGA Transaction Begins**
  @Transactional boundary starts
  All steps atomic - rollback on failure
end note

' === SAGA STEP 1: Validate and Reserve Points ===
saga -> saga: **SAGA STEP 1**\nvalidateAndReservePoints()

saga -> balanceRepo: 5. findByCustomerIdForUpdate(customerId)\n[Pessimistic Lock]
activate balanceRepo
balanceRepo -> loyaltyDB: 6. SELECT * FROM customer_points_balance\nWHERE customer_id = ?\n**FOR UPDATE** [Row Lock]
note right of loyaltyDB
  **Pessimistic Locking**
  Row locked until transaction commits
  Prevents concurrent modifications
end note
loyaltyDB --> balanceRepo: 7. Return locked balance\n{currentBalance: N}
balanceRepo --> saga: 8. CustomerPointsBalance entity (locked)
deactivate balanceRepo

loop For each selected offer
    saga -> offerRepo: 9. findById(offerId)
    offerRepo -> loyaltyDB: 10. SELECT FROM redemption_offers WHERE id=?
    loyaltyDB --> offerRepo: 11. Return offer
    offerRepo --> saga: 12. RedemptionOffer {pointsCost: X, discount: Y%}
    
    saga -> saga: 13. Validate offer:\n- isValidAt(now) - check active dates\n- hasAvailableUses() - check global limit\n- Check expiration
    
    saga -> usageRepo: 14. findByCustomerIdAndRedemptionOfferId(customerId, offerId)
    usageRepo -> loyaltyDB: 15. SELECT FROM redemption_usage\nWHERE customer_id=? AND offer_id=?
    loyaltyDB --> usageRepo: 16. Return usage record
    usageRepo --> saga: 17. RedemptionUsage {usageCount: M}
    
    saga -> saga: 18. Validate customer usage:\nusageCount < maxUsesPerCustomer
end

saga -> saga: 19. Calculate total points cost:\nSum of all selected offers = totalPointsCost

saga -> saga: 20. Validate sufficient balance:\ncurrentBalance >= totalPointsCost ✓

alt Insufficient points
    saga --> controller: Throw IllegalArgumentException\n"Insufficient points. Required: 250, Available: 500"
    controller --> apiGw: 400 Bad Request
    apiGw --> pos: Error response
    pos --> customer: Cannot redeem - insufficient points
else Sufficient points - Continue SAGA
    saga -> balanceRepo: 21. balance.debitPoints(totalPointsCost)
    note right of saga
      In-memory deduction
      Not persisted yet
    end note
    
    saga -> balanceRepo: 22. save(balance)
    balanceRepo -> loyaltyDB: 23. UPDATE customer_points_balance\nSET current_balance = current_balance - totalPointsCost,\n    lifetime_redeemed = lifetime_redeemed + totalPointsCost\nWHERE customer_id = ?
    loyaltyDB --> balanceRepo: 24. Update successful
    balanceRepo --> saga: 25. Updated balance entity
    
    note right of saga
      **SAGA STEP 1 COMPLETE**
      Points reserved (deducted)
      Still in transaction
    end note
    
    ' === SAGA STEP 2: Calculate Discounted Prices ===
    saga -> saga: **SAGA STEP 2**\ncalculateDiscountedPrices()
    
    saga -> saga: 26. Apply offer discounts to basket items:\nFor each item, apply discount percentage\nCalculate total savings
    
    saga -> saga: 27. Build BasketPricingResponse:\n{\n  originalTotal: X,\n  discountedTotal: Y,\n  totalSavings: Z,\n  pointsDeducted: totalPointsCost\n}
    
    note right of saga
      **SAGA STEP 2 COMPLETE**
      Prices calculated
      Response prepared
    end note
    
    ' === SAGA STEP 3: Record Redemption Transactions ===
    saga -> saga: **SAGA STEP 3**\nrecordRedemptionTransactions()
    
    saga -> txRepo: 28. save(PointsTransaction)\n{\n  customerId: customerId,\n  type: REDEEMED,\n  amount: -totalPointsCost,\n  description: "Basket {basketReference}"\n}
    txRepo -> loyaltyDB: 29. INSERT INTO points_transactions\n(customer_id, type, points_amount, source_ref, timestamp)
    loyaltyDB --> txRepo: 30. Insert successful
    txRepo --> saga: 31. Transaction record created
    
    note right of saga
      **SAGA STEP 3 COMPLETE**
      Audit trail recorded
      Transaction logged
    end note
    
    ' === SAGA STEP 4: Update Offer Usage ===
    saga -> saga: **SAGA STEP 4**\nupdateOfferUsage()
    
    loop For each redeemed offer
        saga -> usageRepo: 32. Increment usage count
        usageRepo -> loyaltyDB: 33. UPDATE redemption_usage\nSET usage_count = usage_count + 1\nWHERE customer_id=? AND offer_id=?
        loyaltyDB --> usageRepo: 34. Update successful
        usageRepo --> saga: 35. Updated usage
        
        saga -> offerRepo: 36. Decrement global offer uses
        offerRepo -> loyaltyDB: 37. UPDATE redemption_offers\nSET current_uses = current_uses + 1\nWHERE id=?
        loyaltyDB --> offerRepo: 38. Update successful
        offerRepo --> saga: 39. Updated offer
    end
    
    note right of saga
      **SAGA STEP 4 COMPLETE**
      Usage limits updated
      All SAGA steps successful!
    end note
    
    note right of saga
      **SAGA Transaction Commits**
      All database changes persist
      Lock released
    end note
    
    deactivate saga
    
    saga --> controller: 40. Return BasketPricingResponse
    controller --> apiGw: 41. 200 OK + Pricing response
    apiGw --> pos: 42. Discounted prices
    pos --> customer: 43. Checkout complete\nSaved {totalSavings} with {pointsDeducted} points
end

|||

== SAGA Compensation: Failure During Transaction ==

customer -> pos: 44. Checkout attempt with invalid offer
pos -> apiGw: 45. POST /api/loyalty/basket/price\n{selectedOfferIds: [{expiredOfferId}]}
apiGw -> controller: 46. Forward request
controller -> saga: 47. priceBasketWithRedemption(request)
activate saga

saga -> balanceRepo: 48. findByCustomerIdForUpdate() [Lock acquired]
balanceRepo -> loyaltyDB: 49. SELECT FOR UPDATE
loyaltyDB --> balanceRepo: 50. Return locked balance
balanceRepo --> saga: 51. Balance (locked)

saga -> offerRepo: 52. findById(offerId)
offerRepo -> loyaltyDB: 53. SELECT FROM redemption_offers WHERE id=?
loyaltyDB --> offerRepo: 54. Return offer
offerRepo --> saga: 55. Offer {validUntil: {pastDate}, expired}

saga -> saga: 56. Validate: isValidAt(now)\ncurrentDate > validUntil ✗

note right of saga
  **SAGA Failure Detected**
  Offer expired!
end note

saga --> saga: 57. Throw IllegalArgumentException\n"Offer expired or inactive: {offerId}"

note right of saga
  **@Transactional Rollback**
  All database changes reverted:
  - Lock released
  - No points deducted
  - No transactions recorded
  - No usage updated
  
  **Compensation Automatic**
  No manual cleanup needed
end note

deactivate saga

saga --> controller: 58. Exception propagated
controller --> apiGw: 59. 400 Bad Request\n"Offer expired or inactive: {offerId}"
apiGw --> pos: 60. Error response
pos --> customer: 61. Redemption failed - offer expired

@enduml
